# <%= it.scope.slice(1) %>-<%= it.options.name %>

A remote of a polyrepo made with [mfeflow](https://github.com/mfeflow/mfeflow). It exposes `./App`
and is deployed on its own. The shell lives in its own repo.

```
apps/<%= it.options.name %>   the remote
```

## Run it

```sh
pnpm install
pnpm dev
```

`pnpm dev` serves the remote on its own port. To see it inside the shell, run `pnpm dev` in the shell
repo too: the shell's dev config lists this remote's dev server.

## Deploy it

Each remote is deployed on its own. The registry entries live in the shell repo, not here. See
"Deploy and roll back" in the mfeflow docs for the commands.
